@page
@model Htmxmas.Pages.Samples.Day_11.IndexModel

@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Day 11: Are You Sure About That?";
}

<div class="row">
    <div class="col-6">
        <markdown>
            # Day 11: Are You Sure About That?

            Sometimes you want to make sure that the user really wants to do something, especially if it's a destructive
            action.
            This is where the `hx-confirm` attribute comes in. By adding `hx-confirm` to any Htmx element, you can
            specify a message that will be displayed to the user before the action is taken. If the user confirms, the
            action is taken. If the user cancels, the action is not taken.

            This can help save your users from accidentally doing something they didn't mean to do.

            ## How Does This Work?
            
            Add a `hx-confirm` attribute to any Htmx element along with a message. The user will be prompted to
            either confirm or cancel the action. It's that simple. The prompt is the browser's native `confirm()` dialog.

            In htmx 4, attributes are no longer inherited by child elements unless you opt in. If you put
            the confirmation on a parent element, use `hx-confirm:inherited`. Here each button has its own message.
            
            ```razor
            <button hx-get
                    hxn-page="Index"
                    hxn-page-handler="Allow"
                    hx-target="#rudolph"
                    hx-swap="outerHTML"
                    hx-confirm="Are you sure you want to let Rudolph join the reindeer games?"
                    class="btn btn-danger">
                Allow
            </button>
            ```
        </markdown>
        @await Html.PartialAsync("_Paging", new PagingModel(11))
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <div class="card text-center">
            <div class="card-header">
                <h2>Rudolph Really Wants To Play</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body text-center">
                <img id="rudolph"
                     src="~/img/rudolph_sad.png"
                     alt="sad rudolph"
                     class="img-fluid"/>
            </div>
            <div class="card-footer text-center">
                <button hx-get
                        hxn-page="Index"
                        hxn-page-handler="Allow"
                        hx-target="#rudolph"
                        hx-swap="outerHTML"
                        hx-confirm="Are you sure you want to let Rudolph join the reindeer games?"
                        class="btn btn-danger">
                    Allow
                </button>
                <button hx-get
                        hxn-page="Index"
                        hxn-page-handler="Disallow"
                        hx-target="#rudolph"
                        hx-swap="outerHTML"
                        hx-confirm="Are you sure you want to keep Rudolph out of the reindeer games?"
                        class="btn btn-outline-danger">
                    Disallow
                </button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>